/-!
# Explicit columns for a candidate quadratic chart

The first column is (a - 1)e₀. The next twelve are candidate first differences
of the specified orbit words; the final nine span their proposed second
differences. Dual rows supply a left inverse, checked in `Coordinates`.

These are numerical data, not an assertion about matrix-group membership.
The separate word-evaluation and full-kernel restriction obligations are not
assumed here. See `source/generate_coordinates.py` for the untrusted arithmetic
and `source/README.md` for conventions and the outstanding obligations.
Source motivation: GLS3, Table 5.3i, printed p.270. Matrix/word attribution:
Model.Data and TwoCoreCentralizer/source/README.md.
-/

